# Integrality over ℂ[j⁻¹] forces cuspidal decay of gE₄²E₆

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.eventually_norm_slash_le_of_isIntegral_adjoin_coeffEmb_jq_inv`
(`c7bb4faf-6bfe-592f-aa5c-b6db0facab22`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `232bb036-5066-5027-a94f-46a2abc86ff8`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a natural number, $k$ an integer, and let $g,h$ be modular forms of weight $k$ for
$\Gamma_0(N)$ with $h \neq 0$. Let $X \in \mathbb{C}((q))$ be a Laurent series such that $X$ times
the $q$-expansion of $h$ of period $1$ (viewed as a power series, then as a Laurent series) equals
the corresponding $q$-expansion of $g$; thus $X$ plays the role of $g/h$ in $\mathbb{C}((q))$. Write
$J :=$ [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb ℂ ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) for the
Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}$ obtained from [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=
q^{-1}\cdot(\mathrm{jNum}$ base changed to $\mathbb{Q})$ by pushing coefficients forward along
$\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Let $M$ be a natural
number and assume that $X^{2M}\,J^{M+1}\,(J - 1728)^{M}$ is integral over the
$\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by $J^{-1}$. Then for every $A \in
\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and every real $\varepsilon > 0$, eventually as $\operatorname{Im}\tau
\to \infty$ on the upper half-plane,
$$\bigl\|\bigl((g E_4^2 E_6)\mid_{k+14} A\bigr)(\tau)\bigr\| \le
\varepsilon\,\bigl\|\bigl((h\Delta)\mid_{k+12} A\bigr)(\tau)\bigr\|,$$
the slash actions being those of the image of $A$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ in the indicated
weights.

This is the cuspidal-decay half of the identification of regular differentials on $X_0(N)$ with cusp
forms: integrality of the displayed Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}[j^{-1}]$ is the algebraic form
of regularity at the cusps, and the conclusion says $(gE_4^2E_6)\mid A = o\bigl((h\Delta)\mid
A\bigr)$ at $i\infty$ for every $A \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. It is used by
[`ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_of_isIntegral`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_of_isIntegral).

